 "phrases": [
  {
   "text": "What if every shark on Earth vanished tomorrow?",
   "s": 0.172,
   "e": 2.447
  },
  {
   "text": "Sharks sit at the top of the ocean's food chain,",
   "s": 2.994,
   "e": 4.91
  },
  {
   "text": "but their real power is not eating.",
   "s": 5.301,
   "e": 6.781
  },
  {
   "text": "It is fear.",
   "s": 7.144,
   "e": 7.684
  },
  {
   "text": "Off the coast of America,",
   "s": 8.307,
   "e": 9.366
  },
  {
   "text": "scientists watched the chain reaction happen.",
   "s": 9.556,
   "e": 11.409
  },
  {
   "text": "Big sharks declined,",
   "s": 12.009,
   "e": 12.929
  },
  {
   "text": "and cownose rays exploded to around forty million.",
   "s": 13.18,
   "e": 15.612
  },
  {
   "text": "The rays helped wipe out so many bay scallops that a century-old fishery collapsed completely.",
   "s": 16.205,
   "e": 20.84
  },
  {
   "text": "In Shark Bay,",
   "s": 21.42,
   "e": 21.798
  },
  {
   "text": "Australia,",
   "s": 21.922,
   "e": 22.613
  },
  {
   "text": "tiger sharks do not even need to hunt.",
   "s": 22.909,
   "e": 24.553
  },
  {
   "text": "Just being nearby scares turtles and dugongs away from the seagrass.",
   "s": 25.038,
   "e": 28.351
  },
  {
   "text": "That seagrass stores carbon and shelters baby fish.",
   "s": 28.84,
   "e": 31.416
  },
  {
   "text": "Oceanic sharks and rays have already fallen seventy-one percent since nineteen seventy.",
   "s": 31.954,
   "e": 36.199
  },
  {
   "text": "Take the rest away,",
   "s": 36.762,
   "e": 37.623
  },
  {
   "text": "and the dominoes keep falling.",
   "s": 37.822,
   "e": 39.015
  },
  {
   "text": "And the fish we eat depend on that balance too.",
   "s": 39.553,
   "e": 41.748
  },
  {
   "text": "No sharks,",
   "s": 42.268,
   "e": 42.923
  },
  {
   "text": "no balance.",
   "s": 43.111,
   "e": 43.755
  },
  {
   "text": "The ocean's scariest animal turns out to be its guardian.",
   "s": 44.186,
   "e": 46.902
  }
 ]
